BackgroundRatesTest
└── refreshRates
    ├── given a cycle is already running
    │   └── it joins that cycle rather than starting a second
    ├── given the cached rates are still fresh
    │   ├── it does not fetch
    │   └── when the caller forces a refresh
    │       └── it fetches anyway
    ├── given the cached rates are stale
    │   ├── it waits a random moment before fetching
    │   └── it reports that it is fetching
    ├── given Nym is disabled
    │   ├── it fetches directly
    │   ├── given the fetch succeeds
    │   │   └── it stores the rates
    │   └── given the fetch fails
    │       └── it reports the provider errors
    ├── given Nym is enabled
    │   ├── it never falls back to a direct fetch
    │   ├── given the first attempt succeeds
    │   │   ├── it stores the rates
    │   │   └── it clears any backoff
    │   ├── given the first attempt fails
    │   │   ├── it tears the connection down for a fresh gateway
    │   │   └── it tries again
    │   ├── given every attempt fails
    │   │   ├── it backs off before the next cycle
    │   │   └── it reports the failure
    │   └── given the backoff window is still open
    │       ├── it skips the cycle entirely
    │       └── when the caller forces a refresh
    │           └── it fetches anyway
    ├── given a fetch outlives the worker's idle timer
    │   └── it keeps the worker alive
    ├── given the fetch fails with no error to report
    │   └── it says so generically
    ├── given the fetch throws
    │   ├── it reports the error rather than rejecting
    │   └── given what was thrown is not an Error
    │       └── it still reports something readable
    └── storing rates
        ├── it merges over the existing cache
        ├── given some currencies fail the plausibility check
        │   └── it keeps the ones that passed
        ├── given every currency fails the plausibility check
        │   ├── it stores nothing
        │   └── it reports the failure
        ├── given the held rate is unchanged
        │   └── it is not rewritten
        ├── given spot has left the band
        │   └── it re-pegs
        └── it reports success
